# index.cjs is written as the index file of a package that ships two builds: it replaces its exports in the arm of an `if` that runs; the other arm is dead. Nothing can see the object that its exports would
# begin as, so the file begins without one, as where the store is a statement of the file itself: its exports have one store. With two, Link no longer names the one function that a call of them enters.
# The answers where what the file hands on is called twice, in a loop, by two names or from inside itself, and where the file is seen half loaded: ../../parallel/a-file-replaces-its-exports-in-the-arm-that-runs.
# f4 = the body of index.cjs
# RUN: walk f4:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f4:Body
# CHECK-NOT: = NewObject
# CHECK: = PutModuleVariable
# CHECK-NOT: = PutModuleVariable
# CHECK: Return
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell
# SHELL: 8
# RUN(CLOSED): run-in-shell mechanisms=none
# CLOSED: 8
